---
// DNSSEC's chain of trust: each parent vouches for its child's key with a DS record, starting
// from the root key that validating resolvers already trust.
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 400 452" width="100%" role="img" aria-labelledby="dns-sec-t dns-sec-d">
  <title id="dns-sec-t">The DNSSEC chain of trust</title>
  <desc id="dns-sec-d">
    At the top, a trust anchor: the root zone's key, built into every validating resolver; since
    11 October 2026 that is KSK-2024. Below it, three zone boxes linked by arrows. The root zone
    publishes its DNSKEY and a DS record for .in, a hash of .in's key. The .in zone publishes its
    DNSKEY, which matches that hash, and a DS record for example.in. The example.in zone publishes
    its DNSKEY, which matches, and signs its records: shop A 192.0.2.10 comes with an RRSIG made
    with that key. If any link fails to match, a validating resolver answers SERVFAIL.
  </desc>
  <defs>
    <marker id="dns-sec-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" style="fill: var(--viz-ok)" />
    </marker>
  </defs>

  <g font-size="19">
    <rect x="70" y="4" width="260" height="52" rx="16" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-client-soft); stroke: var(--viz-client)" />
    <text x="200" y="27" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">Trust anchor</text>
    <text x="200" y="48" text-anchor="middle" font-size="16" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">root key, built into resolvers</text>

    <rect x="4" y="88" width="392" height="80" rx="6" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-server-soft); stroke: var(--viz-server)" />
    <text x="16" y="112" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">Root zone</text>
    <text x="16" y="136" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">DNSKEY (signs the zone)</text>
    <text x="16" y="158" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">in. DS = hash of .in's key</text>

    <rect x="4" y="200" width="392" height="80" rx="6" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-server-soft); stroke: var(--viz-server)" />
    <text x="16" y="224" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">Zone in.</text>
    <text x="16" y="248" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">DNSKEY (matches that DS)</text>
    <text x="16" y="270" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">example.in. DS = hash</text>

    <rect x="4" y="312" width="392" height="104" rx="6" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-client-soft); stroke: var(--viz-client)" />
    <text x="16" y="336" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">Zone example.in.</text>
    <text x="16" y="360" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">DNSKEY (matches that DS)</text>
    <text x="16" y="382" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">shop A 192.0.2.10</text>
    <text x="16" y="404" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-ok); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">RRSIG = signature over it</text>

    <text x="200" y="444" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17" font-weight="600" style="fill: var(--viz-bad)">any link broken → SERVFAIL</text>
  </g>

  <g stroke-width="2" style="stroke: var(--viz-ok)" marker-end="url(#dns-sec-arrow)">
    <line x1="200" y1="58" x2="200" y2="84" />
    <line x1="340" y1="170" x2="340" y2="196" />
    <line x1="340" y1="282" x2="340" y2="308" />
  </g>
  <g font-size="16" font-weight="600" text-anchor="end" style="fill: var(--viz-ok)">
    <text x="328" y="190">vouches for</text>
    <text x="328" y="302">vouches for</text>
  </g>
</svg>
